cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Math Playground: interactive visualizations of classic mathematical results"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahvaran
    given-names: Ali Reza
    email: ar.shahvaran@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/arshahvaran/math_playground"
url: "https://arshahvaran.github.io/math_playground/"
abstract: >-
  A client-side web application presenting interactive, parameter-driven
  visualizations of classic results in probability, chaos, and number theory,
  including the Galton board, the central limit theorem, Buffon's needle,
  random walks, Fourier series, and the logistic map. Every simulation is
  seeded and reproducible, and each converges to a value verifiable in closed form.
keywords:
  - mathematics
  - visualization
  - probability
  - central-limit-theorem
  - monte-carlo
  - chaos
  - interactive
  - education
  - webtool
